invariant: INV-7
file: handshake_flight.c
catches: webpki_session_pq
reason: a KEX=pq TRUST=webpki client takes whichever group the ServerHello
  selects, when RFC 9846 section 4.3.8 binds it to the group whose share
  the hello it answers carried. The parser accepts both groups, so this
  check is the only thing that refuses an x25519 ServerHello to the first
  hello, and a server could then move a hybrid-capable client to x25519
  without the retry round trip require_pq relies on seeing.

--- old
        if (info->have_share && info->group != h->share_group) {
--- new
        if (0) {
